WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.592 --> 00:00:15.919
"Say, can you tell me a bedtime story?"

2
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.362
Davy asked Anne, who was watching the sunset from Davy's bedroom window.

3
00:00:20.382 --> 00:00:24.064
"I don't want a fairy story," said Davy.

4
00:00:24.084 --> 00:00:31.047
"Fairy stories are all right for girls, I suppose, but I want something exciting, with lots of killing

5
00:00:31.087 --> 00:00:34.963
and shooting in it, and a house on fire, and interesting things like that."

6
00:00:36.544 --> 00:00:43.810
Fortunately for Anne, at this moment Marilla called out from her room, "Diana is signaling you, Anne."

7
00:00:44.971 --> 00:00:50.315
Anne saw the light flashing from Diana's window and left Green Gables to walk to her friend's house.

8
00:00:51.316 --> 00:00:55.300
When Anne arrived, Diana looked nervous and asked Anne to sit with her.

9
00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.144
"Anne, I've got something to tell you," said Diana.

10
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.361
"And I couldn't wait any longer.

11
00:01:02.381 --> 00:01:04.842
I am engaged to be married!"

12
00:01:07.184 --> 00:01:09.765
Anne felt shocked, and then she smiled.

13
00:01:10.846 --> 00:01:17.810
Fred! Anne knew that Diana and Fred were friends and often spent time together, but she hadn't realized

14
00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:18.690
they were in love.

15
00:01:20.191 --> 00:01:24.514
Anne hugged Diana tightly, saying, "I'm so happy for you Diana!"

16
00:01:25.174 --> 00:01:28.296
Anne was happy, but she also felt a little strange.

17
00:01:30.236 --> 00:01:35.999
She felt as if Diana had gone forward into a new world, shutting a gate behind her and

18
00:01:36.059 --> 00:01:37.479
leaving Anne on the outside.

19
00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:41.101
"What does Diana see in Fred?"

20
00:01:41.461 --> 00:01:42.121
Anne wondered.

21
00:01:42.141 --> 00:01:46.543
"He's nice and friendly, but he's just Fred Wright."

22
00:01:46.563 --> 00:01:54.326
"I'm so happy," Diana said, "but it does seem ridiculous to think that I am engaged!"

23
00:01:55.227 --> 00:01:58.188
"Well what's it like to be engaged?"

24
00:01:58.680 --> 00:01:59.981
Anne asked curiously.

25
00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:05.485
"Hmm," said Diana, acting very much like an adult now.

26
00:02:05.505 --> 00:02:08.487
"That depends on who you're engaged to.

27
00:02:09.088 --> 00:02:14.071
It's perfectly lovely to be engaged to Fred, but it would be horrible to be engaged to anyone

28
00:02:14.151 --> 00:02:16.353
else." Anne laughed.

29
00:02:16.373 --> 00:02:20.776
"Well, that's not much help, considering there's only one Fred!"

30
00:02:20.796 --> 00:02:25.319
"Oh, Anne, you don't understand!"

31
00:02:25.779 --> 00:02:26.420
said Diana.

32
00:02:27.476 --> 00:02:29.077
"It's so hard to explain.

33
00:02:29.858 --> 00:02:31.679
Never mind, you'll understand one day.

34
00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:36.883
Now Anne, I'm going to ask you a serious question, but don't be annoyed.

35
00:02:39.105 --> 00:02:42.947
Do you like Gilbert in any special way?"

36
00:02:42.967 --> 00:02:49.912
"I like Gilbert very much as a friend and not a bit in the way you mean," said

37
00:02:50.093 --> 00:02:51.634
Anne calmly and firmly.

38
00:02:52.354 --> 00:02:54.556
She believed she was speaking sincerely.

39
00:02:57.173 --> 00:02:58.013
Diana sighed.

40
00:02:58.714 --> 00:03:01.275
She wished somehow that Anne had answered differently.

41
00:03:01.295 --> 00:03:04.157
"Don't you ever want to get married, Anne?"

42
00:03:04.177 --> 00:03:07.720
"Perhaps someday," said Anne.

43
00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.622
"When I meet exactly the right person."

44
00:03:10.642 --> 00:03:13.063
"But how will you know?"

45
00:03:13.523 --> 00:03:14.324
asked Diana.

46
00:03:14.344 --> 00:03:16.706
"Oh, I will just know."

47
00:03:17.246 --> 00:03:17.866
said Anne.

48
00:03:17.886 --> 00:03:21.569
"He must be extremely handsome and mysterious."

49
00:03:21.589 --> 00:03:25.972
"People's ideals change sometimes," Diana said.

50
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:29.270
"Mine won't," Anne said firmly.

51
00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.872
"What if you never meet him?"

52
00:03:32.232 --> 00:03:33.033
Diana asked.

53
00:03:33.053 --> 00:03:35.715
"Then I shall never marry!"

54
00:03:36.136 --> 00:03:37.757
was Anne's cheerful response.

55
00:03:37.777 --> 00:03:39.558
"I'll be fine!"

56
00:03:40.679 --> 00:03:41.820
Diana shook her head.

57
00:03:43.261 --> 00:03:47.685
Just then someone knocked on the door, and Diana and Anne got up to answer it.

58
00:03:48.506 --> 00:03:51.468
A very attractive, well-dressed woman was at the door.

59
00:03:51.488 --> 00:03:53.310
"Is this where Mr.

60
00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.651
James Harrison lives?"

61
00:03:55.111 --> 00:03:55.872
the woman asked.

62
00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.621
"No, Mr.

63
00:03:58.641 --> 00:04:04.645
Harrison lives over there," replied Anne, astonished to hear a woman asking for her quiet neighbor.

64
00:04:04.665 --> 00:04:10.349
"Well, I did think this place was too tidy," the woman replied.

65
00:04:10.369 --> 00:04:12.750
"Is it true that Mr.

66
00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.912
Harrison is going to get married soon?

67
00:04:15.892 --> 00:04:17.634
A friend told me he was."

68
00:04:18.754 --> 00:04:21.897
"No, no, I'm sure he's not," said Anne.

69
00:04:23.077 --> 00:04:25.219
"Diana's the only person getting married here!"

70
00:04:25.819 --> 00:04:26.680
Diana giggled.

71
00:04:29.328 --> 00:04:33.291
"I'm very glad to hear that," the woman responded, "because Mr.

72
00:04:33.331 --> 00:04:35.432
Harrison is already married.

73
00:04:36.153 --> 00:04:36.914
I'm his wife.

74
00:04:37.994 --> 00:04:38.975
You look surprised!

75
00:04:40.776 --> 00:04:45.560
I suppose he's been pretending to be a bachelor and is breaking hearts all over Avonlea."

76
00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:48.181
Anne and Diana tried not to laugh.

77
00:04:48.201 --> 00:04:53.785
"I suppose," the woman continued, "that parrot is still there?"

78
00:04:53.805 --> 00:04:57.268
"I think it's dead," said Anne.

79
00:04:58.344 --> 00:04:59.705
The woman seemed glad.

80
00:04:59.725 --> 00:05:02.146
"Really? That's good news.

81
00:05:02.987 --> 00:05:04.047
Good evening, ladies."

82
00:05:04.828 --> 00:05:09.631
With that, she walked briskly down the path and out of the yard in the direction of Mr.

83
00:05:09.671 --> 00:05:10.491
Harrison's house.

84
00:05:11.552 --> 00:05:17.415
Anne and Diana went back inside, discussing what had just happened, and then Anne went home to tell

85
00:05:17.455 --> 00:05:19.096
the surprising news to Marilla.

86
00:05:20.577 --> 00:05:22.798
The next day Anne went to see Mr.

87
00:05:22.838 --> 00:05:25.140
Harrison to find out his side of the story.

88
00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.402
His house looked very different!

89
00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:33.286
The floor was scrubbed, and so was every piece of furniture in the kitchen.

90
00:05:34.206 --> 00:05:37.129
The windows were so clean Anne could see her reflection!

91
00:05:37.149 --> 00:05:41.873
"Sit down, Anne, sit down," said Mr.

92
00:05:41.913 --> 00:05:45.536
Harrison. "Emily's gone shopping with Mrs.

93
00:05:45.636 --> 00:05:49.419
Lynde. Well, Anne, my easy times are over!

94
00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.502
It's all tidiness for me, I suppose."

95
00:05:52.962 --> 00:05:58.090
Mr. Harrison tried to sound sad, but it was clear that he was secretly pleased.

96
00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:02.712
"Mr. Harrison, you're glad your wife is back!"

97
00:06:03.153 --> 00:06:04.013
Anne exclaimed.

98
00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:08.756
"Well, I'm getting used to it," he said sheepishly.

99
00:06:08.776 --> 00:06:12.398
"And I never pretended I wasn't married.

100
00:06:13.198 --> 00:06:14.879
It's just that no one ever asked me!"

101
00:06:14.899 --> 00:06:18.041
"Why did you and your wife separate?"

102
00:06:18.441 --> 00:06:19.062
Anne asked.

103
00:06:19.562 --> 00:06:21.943
"Well, we loved each other," said Mr.

104
00:06:21.964 --> 00:06:28.056
Harrison. "But after we got married, Emily spent all her time cleaning and ordering me around!

105
00:06:28.737 --> 00:06:31.559
I was cranky and hard to live with too, I suppose.

106
00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.361
It was both our faults.

107
00:06:35.083 --> 00:06:37.745
Aside from that, though, Emily didn't like parrots.

108
00:06:39.246 --> 00:06:43.630
She said I had to choose between her and Ginger, and I chose Ginger!

109
00:06:44.931 --> 00:06:49.756
Understand, Anne, that I was pretty angry with Emily at the time, and she was angry with me.

110
00:06:50.548 --> 00:06:55.412
But now we've realized we still love each other very much, so Emily's going to stay.

111
00:06:56.173 --> 00:06:57.894
You have a new neighbor, Anne!"
